From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] feat: simulate job and workload admission via visibility subresource

External orchestrators and autoscalers cannot predict whether a proposed workload will be admitted, queued, or rejected without actually creating Kubernetes resources and mutating cluster state.

Determining admission feasibility in Kueue requires evaluating complex queue hierarchies, cohort borrowing limits, flavor quotas, and active preemption policies. Tools predicting scheduling feasibility historically had to dry-run pod creation against the API server, which cannot evaluate Kueue's internal queue caches and leads to cluster state churn.

Expose a dry-run admission simulation endpoint under /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{namespace}/localqueues/{localqueue}/simulate behind the PreSubmissionSimulator feature gate. Allow clients to POST hypothetical Job or Workload manifests and return simulated admission decisions, flavor allocations, pod set counts, and queue placement reasons without mutating cluster state.
---
